<attribute name="mainDescription" nodeId="89adebca">&lt;p&gt;
    The cutover readiness criteria are metrics against which the organization&apos;s readiness to proceed with the transition,
    or phase will be measured. The criteria provide a measure of how ready the organization is to accept a new solution and
    how ready the program is to deploy it.
&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;
    The criteria should be categorized into broad headings such as:
&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        Processes are proven
    &lt;/li&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        Systems are ready
    &lt;/li&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        Business is ready
    &lt;/li&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        People are ready
    &lt;/li&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        Data is ready
    &lt;/li&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        Technology infrastructure is proven
    &lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;</attribute>
<attribute name="externalId" nodeId="5840da65"></attribute>
<attribute name="keyConsiderations" nodeId="8aadf24c">Once agreed in the planning phases, the criteria should be monitored and updated through the organization or program
governance structure. As go-live nears, the criteria will be monitored daily.</attribute>
<attribute name="longPresentationName" nodeId="818ef4ee"></attribute>
<attribute name="purpose" nodeId="c8ec312f">To allow the organization to confirm that all organizational, business, functional, technical and system aspects have been
considered and are in place prior to the decision to proceed with the transition.</attribute>
